    "answer": {
      "short": "Volunteer (self-selection) bias: people who enjoy surveys are more likely to reply, so people who dislike surveys are underrepresented. The responses cannot show that people generally love surveys.",
      "worked": "Participation is voluntary, so people who enjoy answering surveys are more likely to respond. People who dislike surveys may be less likely to reply, so their views are underrepresented. The displayed percentages describe 499 “Yes” responses and 1 “No” response among the 500 respondents. This self-selected sample cannot establish that people generally love responding to surveys.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
